[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - runtime options / modes / flags: **none.** No setters, no config struct, no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   globals with external linkage, no environment reads, no `#ifdef` build flags
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (the header's include guard is the only preprocessor conditional), and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `translation/Cargo.toml` has no `[features]`. So there is no option axis.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - control flow the C actually branches on: exactly one construct —
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++)` (fixed trip count 10, not input dependent).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **hidden state axis (the real one):** `static int sum = 0;` inside
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `static_sum` has static storage duration, so it is process-wide,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   zero-initialised once, and *mutated by every call*. Behaviour therefore
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   depends on the whole call history, not on the current argument alone. This is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   the axis where interaction bugs can hide, so it is enumerated explicitly
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   below (accumulator sign/magnitude class × call-sequence shape).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **call-hierarchy axis:** `driver` is the convenience wrapper; `static_sum` is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   the lowest-level entry point and is *also* called internally by `driver`, so
