[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Differential-test method (applies to every row)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Both `.so` files are `dlopen`ed in one process, so each keeps its *own* copy of
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the accumulator. Every row drives **the identical call sequence into both
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m libraries in lockstep** and compares after each step, so the rows are
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m order-independent and no `dlclose` state reset is needed:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
