[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    121[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `test … ok` progress lines landed inside a capture window and were mistaken
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    122[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    for library output. `translation/.cargo/config.toml` sets
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    123[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `RUST_TEST_THREADS=1` (forced), so a plain `cargo test` is correct.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    124[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    125[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Harness validation (negative controls)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    126[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    127[0m:[38;5;10m[49m A differential suite that passes is worthless if it cannot fail. Each of the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    128[0m:[38;5;10m[49m following mutations was applied to `translation/src/lib.rs`, rebuilt, and the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    129[0m:[38;5;10m[49m suite re-run; every one was caught (counts are matching failure/divergence lines
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    130[0m:[38;5;10m[49m across the whole suite):
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    131[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
